{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/tbl-tm-notation-table1-data","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Table","doco:Table"],"label":"tbl:tm-notation-table1-data","kind":"table","title":"Data table 1 from tm-notation","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/tm-notation"],"tags":["extracted-table"],"text":"tm-notation-table1-data.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"tbl:tm-notation-table1-data\"></a><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Symbol</th>\n<th>Name</th>\n<th>Definition</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code></td>\n<td>Substrate parameter</td>\n<td>A real number <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q > 1</code> (the single free parameter of the theory)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">s</code></td>\n<td>Skein amplitude</td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">s = q^{1/2} - q^{-1/2}</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">z</code></td>\n<td>Markov parameter</td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">z(q) = \\dfrac{q^3}{q^2+1} = \\dfrac{q^2}{[2]_q}</code> — <strong>convention D</strong>, <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">z(q_0) = 0.61268803714646525160</code>. The excised convention C wrote <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">1/(q^{1/2}+q^{-1/2})</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\sigma_i</code></td>\n<td>Braid / Hecke generator</td>\n<td>Generator of the braid group <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">B_n</code> and its image in <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">H_n(q)</code> (same symbol); in the latter satisfies the Hecke relation <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\sigma_i^2 = (q - q^{-1})\\sigma_i + 1</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">J_K(q)</code></td>\n<td>Jones polynomial</td>\n<td>Knot invariant of knot <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">K</code>, polynomial in <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q^{\\pm 1}</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathrm{M}_2(R)</code></td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">2 \\times 2</code> matrices</td>\n<td>Over ring <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">R = \\mathbb{Z}[q^{\\pm 1/2}]</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathbb{I}</code></td>\n<td>Identity matrix</td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\begin{pmatrix} 1 &#x26; 0 \\\\ 0 &#x26; 1 \\end{pmatrix}</code></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/appendix-transfer-matrices/tm-notation-table1-data.md","heading":"Table"}
